# Step 4 Walkthrough: Batch Pre-generation

I have successfully implemented the background batch pre-generation script to help you proactively generate explanations for your questions and save on API costs.

## What was built

1. **New AI Batch Flow**
   - Created `src/ai/flows/batch-provide-exam-feedback.ts`. 
   - This flow uses a highly optimized prompt designed to take an array of questions (up to 10 at a time) and return an array of concise explanations in a single API request, heavily reducing token overhead.

2. **Background Script**
   - Created `scripts/batch-generate-feedback.ts`.
   - This script queries your Prisma database for all `APPROVED` questions that are currently missing explanations (`feedback: null` or `""`).
   - It iterates through these questions in batches of 10.
   - For each batch, it calls the new AI flow, receives 10 explanations at once, and updates the database immediately.
   - It also includes a built-in 10-second delay between batches to ensure you do not hit rate limits on the free tier.

3. **NPM Command**
   - Added a new script to your `package.json`.

## How to use it

Whenever you add a large batch of new questions to your database via the Admin panel, you can open your terminal and run:

```bash
npm run generate-feedback
```

The script will automatically detect any questions missing explanations, process them in batches, and save the AI-generated feedback directly to your database. Once it finishes, all your users will instantly see the explanations in-game without ever triggering the AI API themselves!
